 {"id":"RELEASE-001","status":"pending","priority":"P1","type":"task","complexity":3,"title":"P1 [releng] SpecLang release readiness - NO-GO at b9bb5042 (4 blocking gates; candidate 1.1.0 proposed)","reasoning":"Rolling release-readiness row, first pass of the speclang-releng lane on this board. Certified candidate = origin/main b9bb5042145f9a87de26c667b1b774adde6a0297, re-read from the release-authority remote origin = github.com/dexdat/SpecLang (default branch main per gh repo view; PUBLIC). Census f7b4ce7d..b9bb5042 (baseline = main-lineage commit the local v1.0.0 peels to): 723 no-merge commits, 6 merges, strict parser reconciles 668 conventional + 55 non-conventional = 723. Type buckets chore 377, speclang 91, docs 64, fix 49, board 43, dogfood 10, ci 9, test 6, feat 4. Breaking changes 0. Material split by changed paths: 173 commits touch product paths, 470 bookkeeping-only, 80 residual. Bump rule gives MINOR -> 1.1.0 proposed, NOT authorized. CI on candidate: run 43855424821 exact-SHA success, job Build-test-and-guard all executed steps success; Tier 2 LLM review skipped BY DESIGN (workflow condition is pull_request or develop push). GitReins Tier 1 guard passed inside that CI job; no Tier 2 verdict exists (no .gitreins/history, tasks.yaml last touched 2026-09-26) so GitReins is degraded, not release-grade. DECISION NO-GO on four independent gates: (a) channel - npm name speclang is owned by a third-party publisher (maintainer speclang <speclangdev@gmail.com>, created 2022-05-13, source github.com/Specific-Language/speclang), npm whoami ENEEDAUTH, gh actions secrets total_count=0, and gh release list is EMPTY so the forge Release channel has never published (any cut is a first publication and needs owner authorization); (b) artifact - installing the packed tarball in a clean consumer exits 127 with bash scripts/postinstall-lint-deps.sh No such file or directory because files[] ships 0 scripts/ entries while package.json declares that postinstall, tarball sha2